# vega: a working program inside a Vasarely swell
#
# The eye pushes 5, prints it, and halts on the void at (2,0) -- three cells,
# top left. Every other cell on the plate is a disc, which is to say a PUSH
# instruction, and none of them ever executes.
#
# Their scales are a radial gradient: largest at the centre, smallest at the
# corners, so the flat lattice reads as a sphere bulging toward the viewer.
# That is the Vega effect, and it costs nothing semantically -- a cell's scale
# is read only by the PUSH family on the cell the eye is standing on, and by a
# get aimed at its coordinates. This plate uses no get and the eye visits three
# cells, so all 253 remaining scales are free composition.
#
# The three program cells are visible as a disturbance in the top-left of the
# field: the code is where the swell breaks.
#
# Ground is cream (1) throughout and every form colour is black (0). A swell
# wants a tight palette -- varied grounds would compete with the gradient
# rather than support it.
%plate 16x16

o.51  +..1  ...1  o.11  o.21  o.21  o.21  o.21  o.21  o.21  o.21  o.21  o.11  o.11  o..1  o..1
o..1  o.11  o.11  o.21  o.21  o.21  o.31  o.31  o.31  o.31  o.21  o.21  o.21  o.11  o.11  o..1
